.TH CHANGELOG-LINT-CHANGELOG-YAML 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog lint\-changelog\-yaml \- validate changelog.yaml configuration file syntax and structure
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog lint\-changelog\-yaml
\fICHANGELOG_YAML_PATH\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBlint\-changelog\-yaml\fR command validates the syntax, structure, and field values of a changelog.yaml configuration file. It checks for common errors like invalid YAML formatting, missing required fields, incorrect data types, and unsupported options.

This is essential before running release or generate commands to ensure the configuration is valid and will produce expected output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Enable strict validation with additional checks:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Complain about extra entries not in changelog.yaml spec (unknown fields)
.IP \(bu 2
Validate all referenced directories exist
.IP \(bu 2
Check for deprecated or conflicting option combinations
.RE

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-semantic\-versioning\fR
Assume use_semantic_versioning=false in the changelog config. Disables semver enforcement during validation.
.SH REQUIRED FIELDS VALIDATED
.PP
The linter checks for these essential configuration fields:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtitle\fR \- Project title (required, string)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBversion_pattern\fR \- Regex pattern for version validation (optional but recommended)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBkeep_fragments\fR \- Boolean controlling fragment retention after release
.RE

.TP
.B Supported Field Types:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Strings: title, codename, changelog_filename_template
.IP \(bu 2
Booleans: keep_fragments, is_other_project, sanitize_changelog, use_fqcn
.IP \(bu 2
Integers: changelog_filename_version_depth, page_size (for log command)
.IP \(bu 2
Arrays: output_formats, templates, notes_dirs
.IP \(bu 2
Maps: sections (category to display name mapping), custom_templates
.RE

.TP
.B Common Validation Errors:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIMissing title field\fR \- Required for all changelog configurations
.IP \(bu 2
\fIInvalid version_pattern regex\fR \- Regex syntax errors in pattern definition
.IP \(bu 2
\fIBad data types\fR \- String where integer expected, boolean where string required
.IP \(bu 2
\fIUnknown fields\fR \- Options not recognized by current changelog version
.IP \(bu 2
\fIDeprecated options\fR - Legacy settings that should be updated
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Validate default changelog.yaml in current directory:
.nf
    changelog lint-changelog-yaml changelogs/config.yaml
.fi

.TP
Run strict validation with additional checks:
.nf
    changelog lint-changelog-yaml --strict changelogs/config.yaml
.fi

.TP
Validate configuration without semver enforcement:
.nf
    changelog lint-changelog-yaml --no-semantic-versioning custom-config.yaml
.fi

.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
\fB0\fR
Configuration file is valid with no errors.

.TP
\fB1\fR
Validation errors found. Output lists each error with field name and description.

.TP
\fB2\fR
Internal error (file not found, permission denied, parse failure).
.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
\fBchangelog-config(5)\fR \- Complete configuration reference with all options
.TP
\fBchangelog-reformat(8)\fR \- Reformat and normalize configuration files
